# Cloudflare Pages header rules.
#
# No build step here means no content-hashed filenames — app.js today and
# app.js after a fix are the same URL. Without this, the CDN edge (or the
# browser's own HTTP cache) is free to keep serving a fixed response for a
# while, which would silently delay both the service worker's own update
# check on sw.js and every network-first fetch() it makes for the rest of
# the app shell. `no-cache` still allows conditional revalidation (304s),
# it just forbids serving a cached copy without checking first.
#
# Content-Security-Policy:
#   script-src is 'self' plus 'wasm-unsafe-eval' — every script is a same-
#   origin file (src/app.js, vendor/qrcode.js, src/preinit.js), no inline
#   scripts left (see src/preinit.js's own comment on why that one was moved
#   out of index.html rather than covered by a content hash here), but
#   'wasm-unsafe-eval' is load-bearing: WebAssembly.instantiate() (how
#   wallet_wasm.js boots the actual signing engine) is blocked by CSP without
#   it, same as eval() would be — confirmed by testing this exact policy
#   locally, where its absence silently broke wallet creation entirely
#   (caught by app.js's own error screen, not a visible CSP console message).
#   style-src needs 'unsafe-inline': the hand-rolled `el()` helper sets
#   plenty of inline `style="..."` attributes — scoping that down to CSS
#   classes everywhere would be a large, separate refactor, and inline
#   *styles* (unlike inline *scripts*) can't run code.
#   connect-src only lists the hosts the app can actually reach today: the
#   hosted edge and the two public-explorer fallbacks (mempool.guide/
#   blockstream.info — swapped from mempool.space 2026-09-13: identical Rust
#   client code reliably timed out reading mempool.space's response while
#   blockstream.info answered in under 1s, and a user separately reported
#   mempool.space itself being unreachable in-browser around the same time).
#   NOTE: this deliberately does not allow arbitrary hosts,
#   so a wallet still holding a pre-existing self-hosted `fortisd` gateway
#   backend (from before the backend picker was removed) would have its
#   connection blocked by this CSP. Nothing has been published to
#   app.fortistechlabs.com yet, so no such wallet exists in the wild today —
#   revisit this if self-hosted gateway support is ever reintroduced.
#   img-src needs data: for style.css's inline SVG noise-texture background.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; connect-src 'self' https://api.fortistechlabs.com https://mempool.guide https://blockstream.info; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
